  "summary": "Hive runs CLI agents (Claude Code, Codex, Gemini, OpenCode, Qwen, and others) as real PTY processes on the local machine, with a browser workbench where an Orchestrator plans and delegates to workers. The Orchestrator is itself a real agent CLI process, not a scripted manager; it dispatches tasks with `team send <worker> \"<task>\"` and workers report back with `team report`. Evidence coverage: 136 of 173 packet slices were shown to the model; the rest were withheld by the prompt budget.",
